          <p class="about-lead">
            DNA carries the information of living beings. Galaxies have a kind
            of “chemical DNA” too, encoded in the emission lines of their spectra.
          </p>

          <p>
            I am a Brazilian undergraduate at Northwestern University pursuing
            Theatre and Physics &amp; Astronomy. My research combines
            observational astronomy, quantitative analysis, and science
            communication.
          </p>

          <p>
            At Northwestern’s Center for Interdisciplinary Exploration and
            Research in Astrophysics, I study high-redshift star-forming
            galaxies with Professor Allison Strom’s group. I have also conducted
            research on JWST’s Little Red Dots at Yale and mentored an exoplanet
            project through CIERA REACH.
          </p>
        </div>

