        </div>

        <div class="projects">
          <article class="project">
            <div class="number">01</div>

            <div class="project-content">
              <div class="tags">
                <span class="tag">CIERA</span>
                <span class="tag">2024–present</span>
                <span class="tag">Galaxy evolution</span>
              </div>

              <h3>How reliable is spectral stacking for distant galaxies?</h3>

              <p>
                Astronomers stack spectra when individual emission lines are too
                faint to measure. I am testing whether the stronger signal in a
                stack preserves the metallicity and gas-density properties of
                the individual galaxies used to create it.
              </p>

              <div class="project-details">
                <div>
                  <strong>Data</strong>
                  <span>26 KBSS and 24 CECILIA galaxy spectra</span>
                </div>

                <div>
                  <strong>Processing</strong>
                  <span>
                    Rest-frame alignment, slit-loss correction, interpolation,
                    and sigma clipping
                  </span>
                </div>

                <div>
                  <strong>Analysis</strong>
                  <span>
                    Emission-line ratios, metallicity, gas density, and
                    comparisons between individual spectra and stacks
                  </span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <details>
                <summary>Read the project abstract</summary>

                <p>
                  Spectral stacking improves signal-to-noise by combining
                  observations of similar galaxies. This enables measurements of
                  lines that may be invisible in a single spectrum. My project
                  quantifies how the nonlinear physical properties encoded in
                  line ratios map onto mean, median, and summed spectra.
                </p>
              </details>

              <div class="links">
                <a
                  class="link"
                  href="Katarina_Andrade_Summer_Report%20(2).pdf"
                  target="_blank"
                >
                  Research report ↗
                </a>

